#[$in title:["Casts"]]
#[$in description:["Explicit cast syntax, target contexts, fallible conversion and cast evidence in Moth."]]
#[$in head:[language_theme_head]]

#[navbar]
#[sidebar]
init_docs_sidebar()!
#[section, $md:
    # Casts

    `cast` converts a value for an immediate concrete typed destination. Its
    target does not infer the source type, and constructor-like forms such as
    `I32(value)` do not convert. Fallible casts follow ordinary error delivery;
    `catch` handles a selected expression locally. See @../progress (Progress)
    for current compiler and backend support.
]

